  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Wednesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: An anticyclone aloft over the Desert\nSouthwest will slowly move westward into Southern California today\nthrough Sunday. The air quality will be unhealthy for sensitive \ngroups at times today due to smoke from area wildfires. As the \naforementioned upper-level area of high pressure creeps closer to \nthe Silver State Friday through Sunday, the heat will build. \nRecord heat is expected in Ely Friday afternoon. Near record heat\nis anticipated in Elko and Eureka Friday afternoon. A Heat\nAdvisory is in effect for most of Northern and Central Nevada from\n11 AM PDT Friday morning until 9 PM PDT Friday evening. Record \nheat is expected in Ely and Eureka Saturday afternoon. Near record\nheat is anticipated in Elko, Winnemucca, and Tonopah Saturday \nafternoon. Record heat is expected in Ely and Eureka Sunday \nafternoon. Near record heat is anticipated in Tonopah Sunday \nafternoon. Heat Advisories will likely be required for most of the\nforecast area Saturday and Sunday. Here are probabilities of\ntriple digit heat for select locations in Northern and Central \nNevada on Saturday, August 1st, 2026: \n\nBattle Mountain - 95%\nCarlin - 95%\nElko - 90%\nWinnemucca - 90%\nWest Wendover - 90%\nWells - 90%\nSpring Creek - 85%\nTonopah - 80%\nEureka - 70%\nEly - 50%\n\nHigh temperatures throughout Northern and Central Nevada Monday\nafternoon will be around five degrees above normal for this time\nof year. Maximum temperatures across the forecast area Tuesday\nafternoon will be seven to nine degrees above seasonal values.\nHigh temperatures through Northern and Central Nevada Wednesday\nafternoon will be around ten degrees above normal for this time of\nyear. Heat Advisories may be required for parts of Northern and \nCentral Nevada Monday through Wednesday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Medium forecast confidence\nregarding smoke from area wildfires causing respiratory issues \nover Northern Nevada today. High forecast confidence in near\nrecord heat in most of Northern and Central Nevada each afternoon\nFriday through Sunday. High forecast confidence regarding a\nmoderate risk of heat-related illnesses for heat-sensitive groups\neach afternoon Friday through Sunday. High forecast confidence in\nheat persisting into at least the middle of next week.",
